Feature: PetStore API CRUD Operations\n\n  # This feature file contains scenarios for testing CRUD operations on the PetStore API.\n\n  Background:\n    Given the API endpoint is \"https://petstore.swagger.io/v2/pet\"\n\n  @create\n  Scenario: Create a new pet\n    When I send a POST request with the following data:\n      | id   | name   | status  |\n      | 123  | Fluffy | active  |\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"Fluffy\"\n\n  @read\n  Scenario: Retrieve an existing pet\n    When I send a GET request to \"/123\"\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"Fluffy\"\n\n  @update\n  Scenario: Update an existing pet\n    When I send a PUT request with the following data:\n      | id   | name   | status  |\n      | 123  | Fluffy | sold    |\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"sold\"\n\n  @delete\n  Scenario: Delete an existing pet\n    When I send a DELETE request to \"/123\"\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"Pet deleted\"\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario: Retrieve a non-existent pet\n    When I send a GET request to \"/9999\"\n    Then the response status code should be 404\n    And the response body should contain \"Pet not found\"